        "original_id": "bfbc7ad2-ecc0-56f2-8bff-dbd65429ff27",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Cher, Brian Higgins, Stuart McLennen, Paul Barry, Steven Torch, Matthew Gray, Timothy Powell, Mark Taylor, Brian Rawling\n- Products: The Very Best of Cher, \"Believe\", Believe\n- Companies: Warner Bros.\n- Topics: songs, albums, singles, songwriting, production\n\nFacts:\n- \"Believe\" is a song recorded by American singer-actress Cher.\n- Believe is Cher's twenty-second album, and \"Believe\" is the title track from that 1998 album.\n- Warner Bros. released \"Believe\" as the lead single from Believe on October 19, 1998.\n- Brian Higgins, Stuart McLennen, Paul Barry, Steven Torch, Matthew Gray, and Timothy Powell wrote \"Believe\".\n- Mark Taylor and Brian Rawling produced \"Believe\".\n- In a 2000 interview, Cher said that she also wrote part of \"Believe\".\n- The Very Best of Cher includes many of Cher's most popular songs, including \"If I Could Turn Back Time\", \"Believe\", \"Gypsies, Tramps and Thieves\", and \"Take Me Home\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
